course: dictionary
lesson: 10664
title: Unlike: showing difference
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unlike is a small word that shows a difference. It means different from, or not the same as. «Unlike mammals, birds lay eggs.» The sentence compares two groups and tells you that birds are not like mammals in this way.
explain: Writers use unlike to put two things side by side so you can see how they differ. «Unlike a playground scrap, many ordinary people, called civilians, lose their homes, their safety or their lives.» The first part tells you a playground scrap is small, and the rest shows that war is much more serious.
explain: Unlike can also describe a person's usual behaviour. «It's unlike her to be late.» This means being late is not how she normally is. Check your meaning by swapping in different from: «It's different from her usual self to be late» still makes sense.
explain: Maths uses unlike too. Unlike fractions have different denominators, so you must find a common one before you can add them. Unlike terms in algebra cannot be added together. Always ask: are these the same kind, or are they different?
fact: Unlike means different from, or not the same as.
fact: The opposite of unlike, when it means different, is like: «Like poles repel each other and unlike poles attract.»
fact: «Unlike» can also mean not typical of someone: «it's unlike someone to» means it is not how they usually act.
fact: In maths, unlike fractions have different denominators, and unlike terms in algebra cannot be added together.
fact: The southern corroboree frog makes its own poison, «unlike poison dart frogs», which get theirs from the ants they eat.
exercise: «Unlike a debate, an ethics bowl does not give teams a side they must defend.» What does unlike show here? | Someone arguing loudly | *A difference between a debate and an ethics bowl | A word for a team | A way the two are exactly the same
exercise: In maths, which pair is unlike fractions? | 2/7 and 4/7 | 1/4 and 3/4 | 3/5 and 1/5 | *1/2 and 1/3
exercise: «Unlike other deer, both the males and the females grow antlers.» What does unlike other deer tell you? | Reindeer never grow antlers | All deer grow antlers in the same way | Reindeer are the same as all other animals | *Reindeer are different from most other deer, because females grow antlers too
test: «Unlike poison dart frogs, the southern corroboree frog makes its own poison.» What does unlike mean here? | Very quick | *Different from | Lost in the mountains | The same as
test: «It's unlike her to be late.» What does this sentence tell you? | She lives far away | Being late is normal for her | She is always late | *Being late is not how she usually is
exam: Which word is the opposite of unlike, meaning different? | *Like | Different | Strange | Odd
